meta {
  name: Reschedule Appointment
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{baseURL}}/v1/house/:house/young-persons/:youngperson/appointments
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  youngperson: 1
  house: 1
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "parent_appointment_id": 123,
    "appointment_type_id": 1,
    "appointment_date": "2026-02-15 14:00:00",
    "appointment_booking_date": "2026-01-01 10:00:00",
    "surgery_name": "City Medical Center",
    "surgery_address": "123 Main Street, London",
    "appointment_reason": "Follow-up checkup",
    "appointment_location": "Main Clinic",
    "notes": "Rescheduled from original appointment"
  }
}

docs {
  Reschedule an existing appointment by creating a new one linked to the parent.
  
  How it works:
  1. Provide the parent_appointment_id of the appointment you want to reschedule
  2. The original appointment will automatically be marked as "Canceled" with a note
  3. A new appointment is created with all the same details (you can override any field)
  4. The new appointment is linked to the original via parent_appointment_id
  
  Required Fields:
  - parent_appointment_id: ID of the original appointment to reschedule
  - appointment_type_id: Must match the original appointment type
  - appointment_date: New date/time for the rescheduled appointment
  - All type-specific required fields (e.g., surgery_name, surgery_address for GP)
  
  Response:
  - Returns success message: "Appointment rescheduled successfully"
  - Returns the newly created appointment with parent_appointment_id set
  
  Note: This uses the same endpoint as creating a new appointment.
  The parent_appointment_id field differentiates between create and reschedule.
}
